      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Open viewing at 10.50am on Saturday 3rd October - please email to register\r\n\r\nBlock A, 55 Castleforbes Square offers an exceptional opportunity to acquire a spacious two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment located in the heart of Dublin’s vibrant North Docklands — one of the city’s most dynamic and desirable urban quarters.\r\n\r\nPositioned on the third floor of this well-maintained development, the dual aspect property offers a sophisticated blend of comfort, and practicality.\r\n\r\nThe bright, open-plan living and dining space enjoys generous proportions and large windows that flood the interior with natural light with a south facing balcony. The kitchen features integrated appliances, ample storage, and fine worktops.\r\n\r\nBoth double bedrooms are beautifully appointed with built-in wardrobes, including a master ensuite bathroom and family bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe property is completed by two storage closets in the hallway and secure underground parking.\r\n\r\nHallway - 7sqm\r\nWooden floors, intercom, access to all rooms\r\n\r\nLiving/dining room - 24sqm\r\nWooden floors, access to south facing Juliet balcony\r\n\r\nKitchen - 6sqm\r\nWooden floors, integrated units\r\n\r\nMaster bedroom & ensuite - 15sqm\r\nCarpet, double window, built-in wardrobe. Shower, WC, WHB\r\n\r\n2nd double bedroom - 11sqm\r\nCarpet, double window, built-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nFamily bathroom - 5sqm\r\nPartially tiled, bath, WHB, WC\r\n\r\nStorage closet - 2sqm\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned in Dublin’s Docklands, this apartment is moments from the IFSC, Spencer Dock, and Grand Canal Dock — home to many of the world’s leading tech and financial firms. A host of cafés, bars, restaurants, and leisure amenities are within walking distance, while excellent transport links include the LUAS, DART, and numerous Dublin Bus routes, offering effortless access to the wider city."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
